From fbc6feace322980bd0eafdf76f2e555574db738d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:11:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008: enable the second I2C
 controller

The Octagon SF8008 carries two demodulators, and each one hangs off a
different I2C controller: the Silicon Labs Si2166D used for DVB-S2X
answers at 0x64 on i2c2, and the AltoBeam ATBM7821 used for DVB-T2/C
answers at 0x40 on i2c1.  Only i2c2 was enabled, so the terrestrial
demodulator could not be reached at all.

Enable i2c1 as well and pin all three controllers to fixed bus numbers
with aliases.  Without the aliases the numbering follows probe order,
which makes an address quoted against "bus 1" ambiguous when comparing
against the vendor kernel.

This only makes the devices reachable; neither demodulator has a driver
yet.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts  | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
index 9fbc643d2100..e97e38ab0eb5 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
@@ -38,6 +38,14 @@ aliases {
 		 */
 		mmc0 = &emmc;
 		mmc1 = &sd0;
+		/*
+		 * Keep the I2C bus numbers identical to the vendor kernel so
+		 * that addresses quoted in the vendor documentation and in the
+		 * tuner probing notes refer to the same controller here.
+		 */
+		i2c0 = &i2c0;
+		i2c1 = &i2c1;
+		i2c2 = &i2c2;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
@@ -186,6 +194,20 @@ &i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The DVB-T2/C demodulator (an AltoBeam ATBM7821) answers at 0x40 on this
+ * bus.  No driver for it exists outside the vendor's binary modules, but the
+ * controller is enabled so that the device can at least be probed.
+ */
+&i2c1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The DVB-S2X demodulator (a Silicon Labs Si2166D) answers at 0x64 here.  Its
+ * RF tuner and the LNB supply sit behind the demodulator's own I2C gate and
+ * are therefore invisible until that gate is opened.
+ */
 &i2c2 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
